# C1-S04 to C1-S07 — the North Field, Field Fracture, the Boar, the Bridge Warning.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1654–1735.
# Refusing to help doesn't end the game: time passes, villagers get hurt, and
# the story carries on through the aftermath. Nobody calls Kaelen a villain.
# rhythm: clipped boar_fight_staged
# (Shouted combat calls during the staged boar fight.)

# C1-S04: the bell rings twice, then stutters.
~ alarm
do bell_alarm
Farmer: The north field! It's split, it's split right down the middle!
do elara_stands
Kaelen: Split how? Like the ground opened?
Elara: You're about to find out. Grab that lantern.
? Kaelen (Internal): She's already moving.
- I'm coming with you. => help
- This isn't my... I don't even know where I am. => hesitate

~ help
set ch1_north_field_helped
do trust elara 10
Elara: Keep up, stranger. And don't touch anything that flickers.

~ hesitate
Mara: Go on. The village can look after itself, mostly. But nobody's going down the south road until that field's sorted, love, so you might as well.
do fracture_spreads
? Kaelen (Internal): It's spreading toward the houses.
- All right. I'm coming. => help
- I'm staying here. => refuse

~ refuse
set ch1_north_field_refused
do trust elara -10
Mara: Suit yourself. I'll put the kettle on for whoever comes back.

# C1-S05: the irrigation water is flowing uphill. Data Vision shows why.
~ field_water
System: SYSTEM TRACE: WATER_SIM RULESET CONFLICT.
System: VERSION A17. VERSION B04.
Kaelen: There are two sets of rules running at once. They're fighting over the same water.
Elara: Can you stop one?
Kaelen: Maybe. If I pick the right one.
Elara: I hate that word. "Maybe" has never once dug a ditch.
? Kaelen (Internal): The sluice. How do I fix it?
- Edit it. Let the current terrain win. => edit_terrain
- Edit it. Wall this channel off from the rest. => edit_isolate
- Leave the code alone. Dig a new channel by hand. => dig

~ edit_terrain
set ch1_sluice_edited
do root_edit sluice terrain_priority
Elara: Fixed? Properly fixed?
Kaelen: For now. Downhill's winning again.
Elara: You say "for now" a lot. I'm starting to notice.

~ edit_isolate
set ch1_sluice_isolated
do root_edit sluice isolate
Elara: The beans are going to be very confused about where their water went.
Kaelen: They're not the only ones.

~ dig
set ch1_sluice_dug
do dig_channel
Elara: You could've done your trick. It would have been faster.
Kaelen: I could've. I'd rather know it works without the trick first.
do trust elara 10
Elara: Huh. That's not what I expected you to say.

# C1-S06: a corrupted boar guarding an erased nest. Data Vision shows DEFEND NEST
# with a null nest reference, the same error as the guardian on the road.
~ boar
Kaelen: It's the same error as the guardian. It's guarding a nest that isn't there.
Elara: Then it's not a monster. It's a mother with nowhere to be a mother.
? Kaelen (Internal): What do we do about it?
- Fight it. => boar_fight
- Turn its aggression down. => boar_calm
- Build it something that looks like a nest. => boar_nest

~ boar_fight
set ch1_boar_fought
do start_boar_fight

~ boar_calm
set ch1_boar_calmed
do root_edit boar aggression

~ boar_nest
set ch1_boar_nest_rebuilt
do trust elara 10
Elara: Moss, sticks, and whatever it is you do. Go on. Make it a home.
do boar_nest_anchor

# Later, at Mara's, if the nest was rebuilt.
~ mara_boar
Mara: I hear you saved a boar. Built it a little house and everything.
Kaelen: It was confused. It just needed somewhere to be.
Mara: So are most of the men in this village, and nobody builds them houses.
Old Fen: Heard that!
Mara: You were meant to, Fen.

# C1-S07: the north bridge is badly fractured. The first explicit deadline.
~ bridge
Bran: North bridge is cracked right through. There's rain coming tonight, and if it's still cracked when the river comes up, it's going in.
Kaelen: How long have we got before the river comes up?
Bran: Until dark. I've written it down, so it's official.
do quest_start bridge_before_dark
? Kaelen (Internal): The bridge, or Aldric's trail?
- I'll fix it before dark. => bridge_fix
- At least keep people off it. => bridge_warn
- It'll have to wait. => bridge_wait

~ bridge_fix
set ch1_bridge_repair_accepted
Bran: Good lad. I'll put it in the ledger as "fixed by the crater".

~ bridge_warn
set ch1_bridge_evacuated
Bran: I'll put a man at each end. They'll complain. They always complain.

~ bridge_wait
set ch1_bridge_ignored
Bran: It's your road too, you know. You walked in on it.

# The bridge outcome is set by the scene at dark: ch1_bridge_saved or
# ch1_bridge_fell. Later caravans, prices and the ending reference it.
~ bridge_saved
Bran: Huh. It's holding. Rain and all, it's holding. That's going in the ledger.

~ bridge_fell
Bran: Heard it go about an hour ago. Sounded like the whole hill sighing.
[if ch1_bridge_evacuated] Bran: Nobody was on it. That's your doing, that part.
[if not ch1_bridge_evacuated] Bran: Tobb's cart was halfway over. He's all right. The cart isn't, and neither's his leg.

# The staged boar fight (no side-scroll arena for it yet).
~ boar_fight_staged
do boar_charge
System: CORRUPTED BOAR — CHARGING.
Elara: It can't turn once it's running! Jump it!
do boar_stunned
Elara: Now, while it's dizzy! Jump, then {move_down} and {attack} on its back!
do boar_pogo
do boar_charge
Elara: Again! I'll wall it in!
do boar_pogo
System: ELITE DEFEATED.
Kaelen: ...It was still trying to get back to the nest. Right up until the end.
Elara: I know. I saw.

# Kaelen stayed in the village. Time passes; the field gets closed without him.
~ field_refused_aftermath
do time_passes
Mara: They got it closed. Bran's lads, the Pell boys, and half a fence.
Mara: Jory's arm's broken. He'll live. He's already telling it bigger than it was.
set ch1_north_field_injuries
